{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35643-picking-a-wod-game-and-the-gmc-and-edition-concerns","id":35643,"title":"Picking a WoD Game and the GMC - and Edition Concerns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T10:01:01-08:00","id":35643,"title":"Picking a WoD Game and the GMC - and Edition Concerns","content":"Hi Folks,<br /> <br /> There was no all purpose World of Darkness forum (and I'm not complaining that there wasn't), so I decided to post this in off-topic, rather than cross-post it in a half-dozen dedicated sub-forums.<br /> <br /> Here we go: I'm interested in some WoD games and but I am a newcomer. I have poked around enough to see that many games use a Core System book, which has been updated with the GMC rules. Also, you can assume I know the difference <i>thematically</i> between cWoD and nWoD.<br /> <br /> I bought Blood and Smoke, and I really like it, but I feel drawn to Changeling the Lost and Promethean. I'm worried however that those games are not updated with the new GMC rules. I poked around their sub-forums and I got concerned. Promethean does have a thread, links to a developer thread, and a lot of discussion about updating it to the GMC, but without buying Promethean, it looks kinda overwhelming. I'm a little put off about buying a game that requires a lot of work to update.<br /> <br /> But that's just it? Does it need to be updated? If doesn't, doesn't that sort of invalidate the intent of the GMC Updates? That is, that Core Rules needed to be fixed up?<br /> <br /> And then there is Changeling: does that require updating to the GMC Version? The thread there is much shorter.<br /> <br /> Then I jump over to W20 and V20. Do they use the GMC Core Version, or as updates to older games do they use a version of rules to existed when they were first published? Again, W20 sounds neat (so did <i>Blood and Smoke</i>), but my eyes keep sliding over to Changeling.<br /> <br /> My pardons for a rambling post. If I were to sum it up in a sentence I'd say, &quot;Some of these games look really neat but I'm afraid to buy one and find out that people have felt the need to really house rule it extensively.&quot; I don't want to learn a new game and try to repair it &quot;out of the box&quot;.<br /> <br /> Any wisdom and/or kind words would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1789,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","user":"Quinarch","date":".  grammar 12-23-2013, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T10:17:53-08:00","id":35647,"title":"","content":"For the nWOD:<br /> <br /> The old books don't need the GMC updates. The GMC updates are generally improvements in the estimation of many (if not most) of the fans, but the old books work fine. They certainly show some age and you might want to look towards books like the GMC or WOD: Mirrors for so ideas on changes, but you can still run the games without the GMC update and have plenty of fun with them.<br /> <br /> Promethean's threads probably a bit busier because the game has a lot of issues that make it both awesome but difficulty; esp. for new WOD players. There's a certain amount of pressure on the GMC update (fan made or official) to solve that.<br /> <br /> Lost is in less of a need of it. Lost has some quirky problems, and could use some of the update (like the social influence mechanics; which don't need any major rules changes to implement), but it has a lot of appeal as it stands.<br /> <br /> For the cWOD:<br /> <br /> The 20th edition books are based on the cWOD systems. They have generally been Revised (aka 3rd) Edition rules with a bit of tinkering and such. They are not really major rules updates (though we'll see when we get into books like Wraith, Changeling, or the later cWOD game lines to see if there's more pressure to do a more significant update). They are intended to be more of an omnibus collection for those games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T10:53:45-08:00","id":35667,"title":"","content":"Thank you Heavy Arms,<br /> <br /> That is very helpful to me. It is especially good to hear that about Changeling the Lost. And if it is simply a matter of implementing the social influence mechanics, I can probably handle that.<br /> <br /> I would welcome further comments! Although if no one else has an opinion, H.A.'s reply has told me basically what I wanted to know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T11:02:31-08:00","id":35678,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms pretty much covered it. The only thing I would add is that while Promethean can seen very overwhelming, it's worth digging into it as it is very interesting and quite rewarding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T11:54:47-08:00","id":35708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35643-picking-a-wod-game-and-the-gmc-and-edition-concerns#post35643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Folks,<br /> <br /> There was no all purpose World of Darkness forum (and I'm not complaining that there wasn't), so I decided to post this in off-topic, rather than cross-post it in a half-dozen dedicated sub-forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think there was one either but its actually at the bottom of the list of sub forums. Just keep scrolling and you'll see it. I think its done that to 5 or 6 people now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:56:51-08:00","id":36116,"title":"","content":"Right now GMC, Blood and Smoke, both the upcoming Demon: The Descent and Idigam Chronicles (Werewolf: The Forsaken's update) use the GMC rules updates. Demon and Idigam Chronicles aren't yet available but should be very soon (Demon sooner than I.C.) If you are a new player I'd suggest getting the GMC rules based books as they were written to update and address some rules issues people had with earlier versions of the games. There would also be less confusion than if you mixed old rule sets with new. There is talk of updating the gamelines outside of the main three (Vampire, Mage and Werewolf) and I would like to see them get updates to bring them in line with the new default setting, especially Promethean since it ties in well with the GMC and is my favorite of the limited run lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}